ion, could push this toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas governor is closer than usual this cycle. Incumbent Republican Greg Abbott seeks a third term against Democratic state representative Gina Hinojosa, and recent polls show a single-digit race, with averages putting Abbott up roughly one to two points. Some surveys, including YouGov and NYT/Siena, even show Hinojosa narrowly ahead, while others give Abbott a four-to-five point edge.\n\nAbbott still holds the structural advantages: a Republican-leaning state, incumbency, and a huge fundraising lead, with $67 million on hand to Hinojosa's $3 million. Democratic groups are debating whether to invest in the state, and headlines describe the race as tightening. Most expert raters call it Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Abbott roughly a 77 to 81 percent chance, suggesting the polls may understate his position.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2248, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.255, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2859, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3188, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3088, "margin":